# R-Stack entry

## Standalone utility exception

A standalone utility request runs only that utility, then stops. It does not start
or resume R-Stack mode or load WORK_PROFILE.md. Preserve a paused engineering task;
continue it only on a separate request or an explicit mixed request.

Utilities are: `bro`, `unslop`, `technical-writing`, `teach`, `how`, `why`, `research`,
`recall`, `show-me-your-work`, `automate-me`, `reflect`, `blast-radius`,
`typescript-best-practices`, `no-comments`, `tdd`, `create-verification-skill`, and
`maintain-verification-skill`. They are available to the model when relevant, not
mandatory phases or automatic post-processing. Select only the skill needed for
the actual request. Do not load the entire toolbox, chain helpers by habit, or
persist a utility's tone beyond its invocation.

Ordinary questions, teaching, explanations, writing and general research do not
require R-Stack mode, even when asked inside a code repository. An explicit request
to use R-Stack mode still opts into it. A mixed request such as "simplify this,
then continue the fix" has two deliverables: do the utility first, then only the
separately requested engineering work. Do not infer the second deliverable from
uncompleted task state.

## Engineering trigger

For actual non-trivial engineering implementation, debugging, architecture,
repository audits or operational changes, load the installed plugin's
`r-stack-mode` skill (the `r-stack` command is an alias) and its WORK_PROFILE.md unless the standalone utility
exception applies. Resolve paths through the host's registry or supplied plugin
root; do not assume a username or a project-relative installation.

The router owns the workflow. Project instructions retain local architecture,
commands, permissions and delivery policy; the host retains executor configuration
and actual isolation. Utility selection never expands mutation authority.

If the plugin cannot be resolved, state that it was not loaded. These are agent
instructions, not a runtime completion hook or a guarantee of model compliance.
